+  // The worker runs kAdvance even when the page is kDeterministicLoading, and
+  // that asymmetry is the point. The coordinator advances the clock to the
+  // MINIMUM requested across clients, so the page's pause-on-load still governs
+  // when time moves. A worker that also paused on its own loads would be a
+  // second brake with nothing to release it: the page is waiting for a response
+  // this worker has to produce. Pausing virtual time does not stop a thread
+  // running immediate tasks, so the worker still serves the fetch, the page's
+  // load completes, and time resumes.
+  const int policy_id = sbxdiff::VirtualTimePolicyFromSwitch();
